            <div xml:id="d209">

                <pb facs="0193" n="183" sameAs="frus:frus1941v06/pg183"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.6363/486: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Uruguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dawson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Montevideo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-11-22T13:00:00-03:00">November 22, 1941—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 22—11:46 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>490. In a note dated November 18 and received this morning<anchor n="15"
                        xml:id="d209-f1"/> the Foreign Office states that Uruguay has decided to
                    adhere to the oil pool. It reserves its decision as respects the coordination of
                    domestic distribution and requests information from the Embassy regarding this
                    phase of the matter. I am in some doubt as to just what the appropriate
                    Uruguayan authorities have in mind and shall discuss the matter with Guani. I
                    have already urged and shall continue to urge the prompt constitution of the
                    national pool committee. Text of code [<hi rendition="#italic">note?</hi>] and
                    full report by air mail.<anchor n="15" xml:id="d209-f2"/></p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dawson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
